---
/*
 * TEMPLATE DOCUMENT — must be reviewed by a UK solicitor before launch.
 * See README.md ("Before you go live") for the full list of legal follow-ups.
 */
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';
---

<Legal
  title="Shipping & Returns"
  description="Dispatch times, delivery, and the circumstances in which VIP Peptides accepts returns."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p class="lede">
    We dispatch within the United Kingdom on a tracked service. Because we supply temperature-
    sensitive research materials, our returns policy is necessarily narrower than for ordinary
    goods — the detail is below.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Dispatch</h2>
  <p>
    Orders confirmed and paid before 2pm on a working day are dispatched the same day. Orders placed
    after that, or at a weekend or bank holiday, are dispatched on the next working day.
  </p>
  <p>
    We dispatch to addresses in the United Kingdom only. We do not currently ship internationally.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    We use a tracked service and send you the tracking reference on dispatch. Estimated transit is
    one to two working days, but this is an estimate and not a guarantee.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deliveries require a signature. If nobody is available, the carrier will leave a card and
    attempt redelivery. Products left unclaimed and returned to us may incur a redelivery charge.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Packaging</h2>
  <p>
    Lyophilised material is stable at ambient temperature for the duration of normal UK transit, and
    ships in insulated packaging as standard. If a shipment requires additional cold-chain
    provision, we will tell you before dispatch and quote for it separately.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please refrigerate or freeze the vials promptly on arrival, in line with the storage conditions
    on the product page.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Damaged or incorrect goods</h2>
  <p>
    Inspect your order on arrival. If any item arrives damaged, with a broken seal, or is not what
    you ordered, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> within
    <strong>seven days</strong> of delivery, with photographs of the packaging and the vials.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where we are satisfied that the fault is ours or the carrier's, we will replace the item at our
    cost or issue a full refund, whichever you prefer. Do not return anything before contacting us.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Off-specification material</h2>
  <p>
    If independent analysis shows that material you received does not conform to the certificate of
    analysis supplied with it, we will replace or refund it in full, and cover the reasonable cost of
    the analysis on production of an invoice. Contact us with the analytical report and the batch
    code from the vial.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Returns we cannot accept</h2>
  <p>
    We cannot accept returns of products that have been opened, unsealed, reconstituted, or stored
    outside the stated conditions. Once a vial has left our custody we can no longer verify its
    cold-chain integrity, and reselling it would compromise the guarantees we give every other
    customer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unopened, undamaged vials in their original sealed packaging may be returned within 14 days of
    delivery at our discretion, provided you contact us first. Return carriage is at your cost, and
    a restocking charge may apply.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Consumer cancellation rights</h2>
  <p>
    We supply to researchers, institutions and businesses rather than consumers, so the Consumer
    Contracts (Information, Cancellation and Additional Charges) Regulations 2013 will not usually
    apply. Where they do apply to a particular purchase, your statutory cancellation rights are
    unaffected by anything in this policy, subject to the exemptions those regulations provide for
    sealed goods unsuitable for return once unsealed for health-protection or hygiene reasons.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds are made to the original payment method within 14 days of us agreeing the
    refund or receiving the returned goods, whichever is later.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Any question about a delivery or a return:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>, {site.contact.hours.toLowerCase()}.
  </p>
</Legal>
